  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Natural Resource Management Capacity in Tajikistan (PAPA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tajikistan):  .This activity will seek to establish partnerships within the Government of Tajikistan and across non-governmental organizations to address Tajikistan&apos;s urgent need for conservation and management of forest resources that are integral to food security, poverty reduction, environmental sustainability, and climate resilience.  The activity will collaborate with the State Forestry Agency to evaluate policies and approach toward rangeland management, rotational grazing, long-term monitoring of pasture and ecosystem health, and develop strategies to address climate-related risks.  The activity will also support sustainable land use practices, such as reforestation and revegetation for enhancement of ecosystem services to prevent soil erosion in high value and/or fragile areas, particularly on hillsides and agricultural fields and establishment of plantations.  This activity contributes to the Mission&apos;s Biodiversity earmark.  By supporting Tajikistan&apos;s climate resiliency, this activity supports ICS Mission Objective 2.1, by supporting improved natural resource management..</narrative>
  </description>
